{"type": "message", "id": "5fc7a81f", "parentId": "74e7379c", "timestamp": "2026-10-08T19:13:13.525Z", "message": {"role": "toolResult", "toolCallId": "call_417d378287c34829aa61ea01", "toolName": "web_search", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "{\n  \"query\": \"2022 NAEP eighth-grade math average score Kentucky 264 Kansas 274\",\n  \"provider\": \"brave\",\n  \"count\": 5,\n  \"tookMs\": 3430,\n  \"externalContent\": {\n    \"untrusted\": true,\n    \"source\": \"web_search\",\n    \"provider\": \"brave\",\n    \"wrapped\": true\n  },\n  \"results\": [\n    {\n      \"title\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"f2640169b6c6ab14\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\n2022 MATHEMATICS STATE SNAPSHOT REPORT KENTUCKY  GRADE 8  PUBLIC SCHOOLS\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"f2640169b6c6ab14\\\">>>\",\n      \"url\": \"https://nces.ed.gov/nationsreportcard/subject/publications/stt2022/pdf/2023011KY8.pdf\",\n      \"description\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"ace53ce24234b9db\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\nNOTE: The NAEP mathematics scale ranges from <strong>0 to 500</strong>. Results presented in this report are based on public school students only.\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"ace53ce24234b9db\\\">>>\",\n      \"siteName\": \"nces.ed.gov\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"title\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"f72db7a31378022c\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\nNAEP Report Card: 2022 NAEP Mathematics Assessment\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"f72db7a31378022c\\\">>>\",\n      \"url\": \"https://www.nationsreportcard.gov/highlights/mathematics/2022/\",\n      \"description\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"8eecc26a6e8be1bb\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\nThe average eighth-grade mathematics score <strong>decreased by 8 points compared to 2019 and was lower than all previous assessment years going back to 2003. In 2022, fourth- and eighth-grade mathematics scores declined for most states/jurisdictions as well as for most participating urban districts compared to 2019. Average scores are reported on NAEP mathematics scales at grades 4 and 8 that range from 0 to 500</strong>...\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"8eecc26a6e8be1bb\\\">>>\",\n      \"siteName\": \"www.nationsreportcard.gov\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"title\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"41b03ce91093d001\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\nNAEP Mathematics: State Average Scores\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"41b03ce91093d001\\\">>>\",\n      \"url\": \"https://www.nationsreportcard.gov/mathematics/states/scores/?grade=8\",\n      \"description\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"ba4eede41ca4e6fe\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\nTo compare average mathematics scores between states/jurisdictions and the nation (public), use the NAEP State Profiles Tool. ... In the 43 states/jurisdictions where scores were lower in 2022 than 2019, <strong>the size of the score differences ranged from 2 to 14 points</strong>.\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"ba4eede41ca4e6fe\\\">>>\",\n      \"siteName\": \"www.nationsreportcard.gov\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"title\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"60c4b920f552ad19\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\nAverage National Assessment of Educational Progress (NAEP) mathematics scale score of 8th-grade public school students, by race/ethnicity, parents' highest level of education, and state or jurisdiction: 2022\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"60c4b920f552ad19\\\">>>\",\n      \"url\": \"https://nces.ed.gov/programs/digest/d23/tables/dt23_222.70.asp\",\n      \"description\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"385983f8946f2642\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\nPrevious Page Download Excel (38KB)\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"385983f8946f2642\\\">>>\",\n      \"siteName\": \"nces.ed.gov\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"title\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"97b616bc0534a